{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what happened before you came in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I stood up from my chair and suddenly the room started spinning. The next thing I remember, I was on the floor. My son saw it—he said I was out for about five minutes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Did you have any jerking movements, bite your tongue, or lose bladder control?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that. I just blacked out. I’ve had seizures before, but this didn’t feel like one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that’s helpful. You also mentioned nausea, abdominal pain, and slurred speech this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the pain in my stomach has been worse since my hiatal hernia surgery three weeks ago. I can’t keep much down—just a little water and a protein shake a day. And this morning, my words were a bit slurred."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s concerning. We’ve given you fluids in the ER and checked your vitals. Your blood pressure dropped when you stood up, which suggests you may have fainted due to low blood volume from not eating or drinking enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it wasn’t a seizure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t think so. Your CT scan of the head and neck showed no stroke or bleeding, and your MRI was normal. Neurology reviewed it and agrees—no signs of a seizure this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But why am I so dizzy and weak?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely from dehydration and poor nutrition. You’ve lost weight, and your labs show you’re not getting enough calories. We’re going to keep you on IV fluids and monitor your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been struggling to eat since the surgery. Everything makes me nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-03-26 16:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. Your history of gastric bypass and recent reversal makes digestion difficult. We’re consulting GI to help figure out the best way to support your nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable, and your blood pressure is improving with fluids. But you’re still having epigastric pain and nausea. We’re going to try a stronger acid blocker."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on omeprazole. Why switch?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting pantoprazole twice a day because your endoscopy showed irritation and a narrowing at the stomach junction. This medication will help reduce acid and let it heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You already had one. Two days ago, during the endoscopy, they dilated the narrowed area with a balloon. It went well, but you’re still not tolerating food, so we need to think about longer-term nutrition support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re considering placing a feeding tube that goes past your stomach into the small intestine. That way, we can give you nutrition without relying on your stomach emptying properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like a feeding tube in my nose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-03-27 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a Dobhoff tube. It’s thin and goes through your nose, down into your intestine. It’s temporary—we’ll see how you do and plan next steps with your bariatric surgeon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-03-28 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your MRI came back normal, which is great news. No signs of a stroke or seizure focus. But neurology still wants to rule out any subtle brainstem issues, so they recommend an ENT visit and autonomic testing after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-03-28 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Autonomic testing? What’s that for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-03-28 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It checks how your body regulates things like blood pressure and heart rate when you stand up. Since you fainted, we want to see if there’s an issue with that system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-03-28 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-04-01 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve been discussing your case with GI and nutrition. Because you’re still not eating and your weight is low, we think it’s best to go ahead with the Dobhoff tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-04-01 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When would that happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-04-01 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow. It’s done during another endoscopy, and they’ll place it past your stomach so food bypasses the slow area."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-04-01 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll get nutrition through it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-04-01 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll start tube feeds slowly and monitor you. The goal is to improve your strength and prevent more fainting episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-04-02 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The tube was placed successfully. It’s now in your small intestine, and we’ve started a slow rate of tube feeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-04-02 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-04-02 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some people feel nasal discomfort, but it usually gets better. We’ve secured it so it doesn’t pull. Let us know if it becomes painful or dislodges."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-04-03 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your stool test came back negative for C. diff, so we can rule that out as a cause of your nausea and diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-04-03 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-04-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. Your dizziness has improved, and your blood pressure is stable. We’ve increased your tube feeds, and you’re getting more calories."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-04-05 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a bit stronger. But will I ever eat normally again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-04-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t know yet. That’s something to discuss with your bariatric surgeon. For now, the tube is helping your body heal and get the nutrition it needs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-04-06 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are improving. Your albumin and electrolytes are normal, and your kidney function is good. We’re proud of your progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-04-06 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m glad I’m not passing out anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-04-07 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge in a couple of days. You’ll go home with the feeding tube and continue the feeds. A nurse will help you set it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-04-07 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need to do this myself?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-04-07 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but with support. A home health nurse will train you and your family. You’ll also follow up with GI, your PCP, and your bariatric surgeon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-04-07 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-04-07 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue all your usual medications—Keppra for seizures, fluoxetine, aripiprazole, and the new pantoprazole. We’ve added sucralfate to protect your stomach lining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-04-08 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on full tube feeds for 24 hours with no issues. Your abdominal pain is milder, and you’re walking without dizziness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-04-08 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’m ready to go home, but I’m nervous about managing the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-04-08 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. The home care team will visit you tomorrow to train you. They’ll show you how to give the feeds, clean the tube, and troubleshoot problems."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-04-09 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The home health nurse met with you and reviewed everything. Any questions before discharge?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-04-09 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if I start vomiting or the tube stops working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2176-04-09 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your GI doctor or come back if you have severe pain, fever, or the tube comes out. For minor issues, the nurse gave you a contact number."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2176-04-09 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2176-04-09 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see GI in one week, your PCP in two weeks, and your bariatric surgeon soon after. We’ve also referred you for autonomic testing and ENT to check the dizziness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2176-04-09 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And neurology?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2176-04-09 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They want to consider an EMU admission later to better understand your seizure history, but that’s not urgent now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2176-04-10 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had another good night. Your vitals are stable, and you’re tolerating the tube well. We’re clearing you for discharge tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2176-04-10 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. Thank you for helping me get stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2176-04-10 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did the hard work. Just keep up with the feeds, take your meds, and keep those follow-ups. You’re on the right path."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. Your discharge papers are ready. You’ll go home with instructions, prescriptions, and your tube supplies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad. Take care, and don’t hesitate to reach out if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Remember to follow up with your bariatric surgeon about long-term feeding options."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll call them this week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. And keep using the lidocaine patch for your knee pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And don’t forget your vitamin D once a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Safe travels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2176-04-11 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-03-26 16:29:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-04-11 12:09:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted following a syncopal episode with no seizure activity, occurring after standing and preceded by dizziness and slurred speech. She had significantly reduced oral intake for three weeks following hiatal hernia surgery, leading to hypovolemia and orthostatic hypotension. Imaging, including CT head/neck and MRI, showed no acute neurological pathology. Chronic abdominal pain and nausea persisted, and an EGD revealed a narrowed anastomotic junction, which was dilated. Due to ongoing malnutrition and inability to tolerate oral intake, a post-pyloric Dobhoff feeding tube was placed, and enteral nutrition was initiated. Her symptoms improved with IV fluids, optimized medications, and tube feeds. She was discharged home with service to continue tube feeding, follow up with GI, PCP, bariatric surgery, neurology, and complete outpatient autonomic and ENT evaluations.",
    "problems": [
      "Hypovolemia",
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Gastrojejunal ulcer, unspecified as acute or chronic, without hemorrhage or perforation",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Nausea",
      "Unspecified abdominal pain",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, not intractable, without status epilepticus",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Vitamin D deficiency, unspecified",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Post-traumatic stress disorder, unspecified",
      "Dizziness and giddiness",
      "Orthostatic hypotension",
      "Pain in left knee",
      "Encounter for immunization"
    ]
  }
}
